\tuplet creates a tuplet following the Lilypond syntax.
Since it concerns rhythmic/melodic lines, it must be
placed inside the notes definition of an instrument,
inside a bar definition.
The \tuplet command can also be called with its
shorter alias, \tup.
Its syntax is the following:

\tuplet 3/2 {c'8 cis' b}

The line above will create a tuplet of three eighth
notes against two.

Inside a bar definition, it looks like this:

\bar tup-1 {
    \time 4/4
    \inst c'4 \tuplet 5/4 {cis'8 b a bes cis'} c'4
}
